# Commit and Push Shorthand

When the user asks “did you commit and push?”, “have you committed/pushed?”, or a substantially similar question after work is completed, interpret it as an instruction to commit the current task’s changes and push the current branch—not merely as a request for status.

- Act immediately unless committing or pushing would be unsafe or is blocked.
- Stage only changes belonging to the current task; exclude unrelated files.
- Never force-push unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Report the commit and push result concisely.
